- Administration now uses existing exact-ID deletion: check authority, admit, then reread actor, exact target/revision, grants, management, and complete active Admin pages before one deletion. Reads stop at ten pages.
- The existing SQL adapter/pool implements the store. Pending intent returns busy; terminal receipts can be replaced. Statements release clients before provider HTTP. Independent provider/operator writes remain a runbook constraint.
- Unknown admission sends nothing. Possible effects retain the hold across restart. While active, known pre-send refusals or proven outcomes settle only their own operation; uncertain completion needs its matching terminal receipt. No lease or replay is added.
- The 30-second lifetime stops later read subcalls and deletion; in-flight WorkOS calls retain five-second bounds. Late replies start no work; already-started terminal SQL may finish for its operation. App stops removal, closes snapshots/clears pending content, then closes Collector/SQL; MCP cleanup runs beside this chain. Recording cannot alter the result or hold.

The green edge is a new runtime call through the supplied store; the opposite type-only source dependency already exists. Seven registry drawings change. [Reviewed renders and provenance](https://github.com/tomer-mayara/Thermus/blob/6181c1750a95cdb7718d7eb351bc1ee55343737d/review-evidence/pr253-rebase-f03a7b73/790fa3e1f85ab3ed9a5228300cc90373117a2793/architecture/provenance-final.json) explain why L3 plus these notes suffices without L4.

**R1 delivery limit:** unused per-member email lookups can exhaust the deadline before DELETE and leave a pending hold. [Controlled latency evidence](https://github.com/tomer-mayara/Thermus/blob/6181c1750a95cdb7718d7eb351bc1ee55343737d/review-evidence/pr253-rebase-f03a7b73/790fa3e1f85ab3ed9a5228300cc90373117a2793/architecture/historical-r1-evidence.md) is not a production benchmark. [PR #257](https://github.com/tomer-mayara/Thermus/pull/257) implements the later repair; it is outside this rebase. Customer removal capture remains S2.5-01c. The rebase preserves feature source/tests and resolves the two document conflicts. [Validation](https://github.com/tomer-mayara/Thermus/blob/6181c1750a95cdb7718d7eb351bc1ee55343737d/review-evidence/pr253-rebase-f03a7b73/790fa3e1f85ab3ed9a5228300cc90373117a2793/VALIDATION.md) retains fresh failures and passes; no merge or production change was performed.

